# apocalypse.vrs: apocalypse Session 1, D25 (the outbreak), D26 (won, lost, survived) and D27 (stop, pillar off, purge).
# apo-test (tools/vrclient/fixtures/apo-test.json, put into the dev events.json): Faction_Undead, units CHAR_Undead_Guardian
# (-1967480038) and CHAR_Undead_GhostMilitia_Light (-1618703048) so that `.devkill` spares the native Farbane skeletons,
# 2 hotspots (minNatives 3, minSpacing 300), roamers 3 per hotspot (+2 per kill, max 12, 4 a minute, huntRange 40), 2 hordes
# from 1 min every 5 min (D1's floor is 5; D25 says 3, see the step 3 report), size 8 growth 4, marchSpeed 3.0, 30 min, and
# a Point goal "the test camp" at (-1188, -1334), 200 m east of the undead site (-1388, -1334).
#
# Holding a front (D6): a front holds while a player stands within 60 m of it, but no hold applies while the front is
# within goal.radius + 60 = 90 m of the goal (so an AFK player at the goal cannot block a loss). Chaos therefore never
# holds at the goal: he stands on a front that is more than 90 m from the goal. A front starts at its hotspot, so Chaos at
# hotspot 1 (`.nyar event info`: "hotspot 1: <region> at <x> <z>") when horde 1 rises holds it at its origin. Hotspot 2 is
# 300 m or more from hotspot 1, and Chaos is in one place only, so for every run but the lost one the goal is moved with
# `.nyar event set apo-test action.goal here` (D16) to G* = hotspot 1 + 200 m along the line from hotspot 2 through
# hotspot 1 (computed with `calc` from run A's hotspots): still 200 m from hotspot 1, as D25 asks, on the far side of it
# from hotspot 2. Horde 1 then holds at its origin, 200 m from G*, and horde 2 marches from hotspot 2 straight at Chaos and
# holds 60 m short of him, 260 m from G*: both fronts held from one place, which is what lets the survived run last its
# 30 min. Each run checks the hotspots are still run A's (within 30 m) and reads the fronts' x, z and % from
# `event info` ("horde <k> front at <x> <z>, <p> %"): a held front keeps its %. G* only has to be a point Chaos can
# teleport to; no unit ever goes there. The lost run keeps the fixture goal: Chaos at the pond holds nothing (checked: 300 m
# or more from both hotspots, 200 m or more from the goal) and horde 1 reaches the goal in about 70 s. The fixture goal and
# speed are set at the start and the goal is set back at the end.
#
# Runs: (A) lost, with the roam check (D25); (B) won, with D25's hotspot, debug and spread checks at hotspot 1; (C) stop at
# horde 2; (D) pillar spawns off at horde 2; (E) survived, Chaos at hotspot 1 for the full 30 min, not attacking; (F) purge
# at horde 2, last, for its cooldown. Natives: `.devunits ${UNATIVE} 60` at the undead site before run A and after run F
# must give the same n (stands in for D25's `.nyar debug natives`, which the mod lacks: see the step 3 report); the
# state.json read after the purge (no "Apocalypse" key) is done by hand on the server copy. About 80 min.
# Needs: a Release DLL with the step 3 review fixes; NyarDevTools (.devgo, .devtp, .devmark, .devdie, .devkill, .devunits)
# and DevChatEcho; vrclient with `calc` and `expect-calc`; apo-test enabled, zombie-apocalypse and every other spawning
# definition disabled; [Scoreboard] IncludeAdmins = true; no purge cooldown; the pond mark; Chaos invulnerable
# (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, never false; a death resets it, so it is set again after each respawn).
# Run: --var UX=-1388 --var UZ=-1334 --var UNATIVE=-837329073
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
# the fixture goal and speed, whatever an earlier run left
chat .devtp -1188 -1334
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.goal here
expect-reply apo-test action.goal =
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.marchSpeed 3.0
expect-reply apo-test action.marchSpeed =
# natives at the undead site before any run
chat .devtp ${UX} ${UZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 5
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devunits ${UNATIVE} 60
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=(?P<NATIVES>[0-9]+)
#
# A. lost (D26): Chaos at the wait spot (--var WX WZ, e.g. -1690 -1400, the stalker camp; the pond is too near a
# Farbane hotspot) holds nothing; the roamers find him (D25) and horde 1 takes the fixture goal
chat .devtp ${WX} ${WZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<PX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<PZ>-?[0-9.]+)
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test hotspots: 2 \( timeout=10
expect-log apocalypse apo-test roam: hotspot [12] on a player timeout=120
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )hotspot 1: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<H1X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<H1Z>-?[0-9]+) \\n hotspot 2: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<H2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<H2Z>-?[0-9]+) timeout=10
# D25's roam condition and an unobserved march: the pond is 300 m or more from both hotspots and 200 m or more from the goal
expect-calc hypot(${PX} - ${H1X}, ${PZ} - ${H1Z}) >= 300
expect-calc hypot(${PX} - ${H2X}, ${PZ} - ${H2Z}) >= 300
expect-calc hypot(${PX} + 1188, ${PZ} + 1334) >= 200
# the roamers came to Chaos (both unit kinds counted): the mover jumps them 25 m every 5 s while no player is within
# 100 m, then lands them 50-60 m from him and they walk in (session 1: none had arrived after 10 or 20 s). Horde 1 rises
# and marches meanwhile, so its lines are read with expect-seen (a matched line consumes the lines before it)
calc NEAR = min(hypot(${PX} - ${H1X}, ${PZ} - ${H1Z}), hypot(${PX} - ${H2X}, ${PZ} - ${H2Z}))
calc WR = round((${NEAR} - 100) / 5 + 30)
wait ${WR}
chat .devunits -1967480038 100
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=(?P<RG>[0-9]+)
chat .devunits -1618703048 100
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=(?P<RM>[0-9]+)
expect-calc ${RG} + ${RM} >= 1
expect-seen apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
# each 25 % step with its keep-up line, at least 80 % of the living units within 30 m of the front (D26)
expect-seen horde 1 front (2[5-9]|[34][0-9]) % units (?P<N25>[0-9]+)/(?P<M25>[0-9]+) within 30 m of the front timeout=40
expect-calc ${N25} >= 0.8 * ${M25}
expect-seen horde 1 front ([56][0-9]|7[0-4]) % units (?P<N50>[0-9]+)/(?P<M50>[0-9]+) within 30 m of the front timeout=40
expect-calc ${N50} >= 0.8 * ${M50}
expect-seen horde 1 front (7[5-9]|[89][0-9]) % units (?P<N75>[0-9]+)/(?P<M75>[0-9]+) within 30 m of the front timeout=40
expect-calc ${N75} >= 0.8 * ${M75}
expect-seen event apo-test ended: lost \(1 of 2 hordes risen\) timeout=60
expect-chat the test camp has fallen timeout=20
shot chat apo-lost
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
#
# G*: 200 m beyond hotspot 1 on the line from hotspot 2, the goal of every later run
calc DX = ${H1X} - ${H2X}
calc DZ = ${H1Z} - ${H2Z}
calc SPACING = hypot(${DX}, ${DZ})
expect-calc ${SPACING} >= 290
calc GX = ${H1X} + 200 * ${DX} / ${SPACING}
calc GZ = ${H1Z} + 200 * ${DZ} / ${SPACING}
# the wait for horde 2 to march from hotspot 2 to 60 m short of hotspot 1 at 3 m/s, plus 20 s
calc W2 = round((${SPACING} - 60) / 3 + 20)
chat .devtp ${GX} ${GZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.goal here
expect-reply apo-test action.goal =
#
# B. won (D26), with D25's checks at hotspot 1: Chaos holds horde 1 at its origin and kills it, then holds horde 2 60 m
# short of him and kills it
chat .devtp ${H1X} ${H1Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test hotspots: 2 \( timeout=10
expect-log apocalypse apo-test roamers: \+3 at hotspot 1 timeout=20
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )hotspot 1: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<B1X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<B1Z>-?[0-9]+) \\n hotspot 2: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<B2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<B2Z>-?[0-9]+) timeout=10
expect-calc hypot(${B1X} - ${H1X}, ${B1Z} - ${H1Z}) <= 30 and hypot(${B2X} - ${H2X}, ${B2Z} - ${H2Z}) <= 30
wait 3
chat .nyar debug here 60
expect-reply CHAR_Undead_
shot full apo-hotspot1
# D25 spread: a roamer kills Chaos; two roamers rise within 3 m of the death point, counted at once (6 m, both kinds)
# before the roam can move them
chat .devmark apo-death
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] apo-death
mark
chat .devdie -1967480038,-1618703048 60
expect-log \[DEV DIE\] found=1 timeout=10
expect-log apocalypse apo-test spread: \+2 \( timeout=20
wait 2
chat .devunits -1967480038 6 apo-death
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=(?P<SG>[0-9]+)
chat .devunits -1618703048 6 apo-death
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=(?P<SM>[0-9]+)
expect-calc ${SG} + ${SM} >= 2
# the respawn is a held space; horde 1 rises a minute in, often while Chaos respawns, so its line is read before the
# teleport's (a matched line consumes the lines before it: session 1 missed it after the teleport)
hold space 1.5
wait 3
respawn-coffin 15
wait 10
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
expect-seen apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
chat .devtp ${H1X} ${H1Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
expect-chat a horde of 8 rises timeout=20
shot chat apo-horde1-rise
# Chaos stands on horde 1's front (re-read, in case it moved while he respawned) and it holds: its % does not change
wait 3
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 1 front at (?P<F1X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<F1Z>-?[0-9]+), [0-9]+ % timeout=10
chat .devtp ${F1X} ${F1Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 1 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<B1A>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
wait 20
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 1 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<B1B>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
# held where Chaos stands; it may have marched while he respawned, but not to the goal margin (200 m, 90 m margin)
expect-calc ${B1B} == ${B1A} and ${B1A} <= 50
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
wait 5
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
wait 5
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 1 of 2 destroyed timeout=30
expect-chat horde 1 of 2 destroyed timeout=20
# horde 2 (12 units) rises at hotspot 2 six minutes in and marches at Chaos at hotspot 1, holding 60 m short of him
chat .devtp ${H1X} ${H1Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 2/2 rose at hotspot 2: 12 units timeout=330
expect-chat a horde of 12 rises timeout=20
wait ${W2}
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 2 front at (?P<F2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<F2Z>-?[0-9]+), (?P<B2A>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc hypot(${F2X} - ${H1X}, ${F2Z} - ${H1Z}) <= 61
wait 15
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 2 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<B2B>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc ${B2B} == ${B2A}
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
wait 5
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
wait 5
chat .devkill -1967480038 400
chat .devkill -1618703048 400
# any unit left (a straggler the game keeps disabled far from players is out of .devkill's reach): logged for the record
chat .devunits -1967480038 2000
chat .devunits -1618703048 2000
expect-log event apo-test ended: won \(2 of 2 hordes risen\) timeout=60
expect-log event apo-test scoreboard: 1 players, [0-9]+ kills timeout=10
expect-chat the living have won timeout=20
shot chat apo-won
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
#
# C. stop at horde 2 (D27): Chaos at hotspot 1 holds horde 1; the stop comes 5 s after horde 2 rises; the scoreboard,
# then 0 tracked after the grace
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 2/2 rose at hotspot 2: 12 units timeout=330
wait 5
chat .nyar event stop apo-test
expect-log event apo-test stopped
expect-log event apo-test scoreboard: timeout=10
shot chat apo-stop
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
#
# D. pillar spawns off at horde 2 (D27): no scoreboard, 0 tracked
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 2/2 rose at hotspot 2: 12 units timeout=330
wait 5
chat .nyar pillar spawns off
expect-reply spawns
expect-no-log scoreboard: timeout=10
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
chat .nyar pillar spawns on
expect-reply spawns
wait 3
#
# E. survived (D26): Chaos stays at hotspot 1, invulnerable and not attacking, for the full 30 min; horde 1 holds at its
# origin and horde 2 holds 60 m short of him, both more than 90 m from G*
chat .devtp ${H1X} ${H1Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )hotspot 1: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<E1X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<E1Z>-?[0-9]+) \\n hotspot 2: [A-Za-z' ]+? at (?P<E2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<E2Z>-?[0-9]+) timeout=10
expect-calc hypot(${E1X} - ${H1X}, ${E1Z} - ${H1Z}) <= 30 and hypot(${E2X} - ${H2X}, ${E2Z} - ${H2Z}) <= 30
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
wait 10
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 1 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<E1A>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc ${E1A} <= 5
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 2/2 rose at hotspot 2: 12 units timeout=330
wait ${W2}
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 1 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<E1B>[0-9]+) %.*?horde 2 front at (?P<EF2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<EF2Z>-?[0-9]+), (?P<E2A>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc ${E1B} == ${E1A}
expect-calc hypot(${EF2X} - ${H1X}, ${EF2Z} - ${H1Z}) <= 61
wait 60
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] |\\n )horde 2 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<E2B>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc ${E2B} == ${E2A}
shot full apo-survive-held
# 15 min with neither a win nor a loss (it ends before the 30 min are up, so the survived line is not drained here)
expect-no-log event apo-test ended: (won|lost) timeout=900
expect-log event apo-test ended: survived \(2 of 2 hordes risen\) timeout=700
expect-chat the living held out timeout=20
shot chat apo-survived
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
#
# F. purge at horde 2 (D27): no scoreboard, 0 tracked, the record gone (state.json read by hand); last, for its cooldown
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 1/2 rose at hotspot 1: 8 units timeout=90
expect-log apocalypse apo-test horde 2/2 rose at hotspot 2: 12 units timeout=330
wait 5
chat .nyar purge
wait 2
chat .nyar purge confirm
expect-log purge: 1 events ended, [0-9]+ units queued
expect-no-log scoreboard: timeout=10
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
# natives at the undead site after the last end: the same n as before run A
chat .devtp ${UX} ${UZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 5
chat .devunits ${UNATIVE} 60
expect-log \[DEV UNITS\] n=${NATIVES}( |$)
# the fixture goal back
chat .devtp -1188 -1334
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.goal here
expect-reply apo-test action.goal =
console TPHome
